@page "/projects/blazor-app/overview"
@page "/projects/game-development/overview"

<div class="project-page page-content">
	<header class="project-header">
		<p class="eyebrow">Game Development</p>
		<h1>Overview</h1>
		<p class="tagline">Unity game design backed by professional software engineering, API integration, and cloud delivery.</p>
	</header>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Game Development Background</h2>
		<p>
			My path into software started with games. I graduated from Kennesaw State University with a Bachelor of Science in Computer Game Design and Development, then carried that systems-minded game background into professional C#, .NET, frontend, backend, and Azure work.
		</p>
		<p>
			That mix matters: game development taught me to think in loops, feedback, interaction, constraints, player experience, and performance. Professional engineering sharpened the other half of the craft: APIs, data boundaries, cloud services, testing, deployment, and maintainable architecture.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Current Direction</h2>
		<div class="project-grid">
			<article>
				<h3>Unity & C#</h3>
				<p>Core gameplay systems, UI flow, mobile release work, platform constraints, and iterative tuning.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>API Utilization</h3>
				<p>Using external data and custom service layers to support gameplay features that reach beyond a local-only game loop.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Azure Services</h3>
				<p>Applying cloud hosting, secret-backed configuration, and operational habits from web engineering to game-adjacent services.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Independent Shipping</h3>
				<p>Owning the path from prototype to published App Store release, including build, polish, submission, and follow-through.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Active Work</h2>
		<p>
			My active game project is <strong>Versus With Verses</strong>, an in-progress Unity project that brings together game design, API-driven content, and Azure-backed services. It is the clearest overlap between my game design foundation and my current backend/cloud specialty.
		</p>
	</section>
</div>
